hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1412","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Hajjaj told us, Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: He drew water like this, and stretched out his hands, and made its interior close to the ground, until I saw the whites of his armpits.”"
"1413","Al-Hasan bin Qazah told us, Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Sulaiman Al-Taymi, on the authority of Baraka, who is Abu Al-Walid, on the authority of Bashir bin Not to mention, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, extending his hands until I saw the whites of his armpits.” Suleiman said: I thought he was praying for rain."
